---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base
  title="Corrections — Gourmet Gastronomer"
  description="How to report an error in Gourmet Gastronomer."
  permalink="/corrections/"
  crumbs={[{ name: "Corrections", url: "/corrections/" }]}
>
  <main class="home" id="main">
    <p class="eyebrow">Corrections</p>
    <h1>Corrections</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      If a fact is wrong, a source is misread, or a page is unclear, say so.
    </p>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        This is a Git-canonical encyclopedia. The useful report names the page
        (title or URL), the claim, and a better source if you have one. Do not
        send hours, menus, or telephone numbers for atlas pages; we omit those
        on purpose because they rot.
      </p>
      <p>
        Food-safety numbers (canning process times, pathogen controls) are
        changed only against an authoritative tested process. A kitchen
        anecdote is not enough.
      </p>
      <p>
        There is no editorial board to appeal to, and we do not fabricate one.
        Corrections land as commits. A page marked <em>sketch</em> is unfinished
        by design; a developing page is sourced work that a human has not yet
        marked reviewed.
      </p>
      <p>
        Open an issue or pull request on the project repository if it is public,
        or write to the maintainer if you reached this site another way. Until
        then, use <a href="/method/">Method</a> to understand how sources are
        chosen.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
